# cli-routes registry: one CLI per line.
#
# Format:  <plain-name> [flags prepended to every call]
#
# Copy this file to cli-routes.conf next to cli-routes.sh and edit it.
# The installer reads cli-routes.conf when present and falls back to
# this example. Any executable named <name>-real found on disk is
# routed automatically even when the tool is not listed here; the
# registry exists for tools that need prepended flags or that a
# `doctor` run should always report on.
#
# agy ships with --dangerously-skip-permissions because that is the
# flag its agent mode needs to run unattended in a terminal. Treat
# every flag here as your own choice for your own machine; remove it
# if you want agy to prompt.
agy --dangerously-skip-permissions
codex
claude
gemini
opencode
openclaw
